  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Harmonisation of SEAH Data Collection and Reporting</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Objective: To increase transparency and mutual accountability on SEAH and reduce under-reporting by introducing a harmonised data collection and reporting framework which will ultimately improve the response outcomes for victims/survivors. 

Project summary:  Consultations with over 65 organisations in Phase One of the project confirmed the need for a harmonised SEAH framework. This project builds on the work undertaken from the first phase with the intention to increase transparency and understanding of the scale of the SEAH problem in aid sector through the development of a harmonised data collection and reporting framework. The project proposed for funding comprises Phase 2 and Phase 3 which includes the development, testing and launching of the framework, with the anticipation that national and international NGOs, and private sector actors involved in aid sector, will collect the same data sets, apply the same definitions and report SEAH incidents within a harmonised and standardised reporting framework. A harmonised framework will facilitate the means of communicating and addressing SEAH, which will ultimately improve prevention and response strategies across the aid sector, enhance mutual accountability and deliver better outcomes for victims and survivors.

Expected Deliverable:  A SEAH harmonised framework for NGOs from the aid sector, and private sector actors involved in aid delivery, which is aligned with the existing UN iReport SEA reporting system.</narrative>
  </description>
